      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Rect">Rect</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="450" ed="#liebermann"/>[11] Be sædere. Sædere gebyreð, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hæbbe ælces sædcynnes ænne leap fulne, ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> he ælc sæd wel gesawen hæbbe ofer geares fyrst.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="450" ed="#liebermann"/>Sædere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Rect_11.lnote.oe.12"/> (id est seminatori) pertinet, ut habeat unoquoque sementis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Rect_11.lnote.oe.13"/> tempore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#Rect_11.lnote.oe.b"/> I leap fulne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Rect_11.lnote.oe.14"/>, quando semen omne bene seminauerit in anni spatio.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="12" corresp="#wit-b">Be SæDERE . Sædere gebyreð þæt he hæbbe ælces sædcyn|nes ænne leap fulne · ðonne he ælc sæd wel gesawen hæbbe ofer geares fyrst.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="326" ed="#rabin-doml"/><hi rend="italic">Be sædere</hi> Sædere gebyreð þæt he hæbbe ælces sædcynnes ænne leap fulne ðonne he ælc sæd wel gesawen hæbbe ofer geares fyrst.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="450" ed="#liebermann"/>Vom Säemann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rect_11.lnote.de.1"/>. Dem Säemann gebührt, dass er von jeder Saatgattung 1 ‘Korb’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#Rect_11.lnote.de1.d"/> voll<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Rect_11.lnote.de.2"/> erhalte, wenn er jede Saat gut gesät hat über den [ganzen] Jahreslauf.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the sower. To the sower is due that he receive 1 ‘basket’ [c. ½ (⅔) bushel] full of each kind of seed, when he has sown each seed well throughout the [whole] year.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">Concerning the sower For the sower it is fitting that he have one bucket full of each kind of seed, when he has sown each seed well throughout the year.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="327" ed="#rabin-doml"/><hi rend="italic">Regarding the Sower</hi> For the sower, it is appropriate that he have one full bucket of each variety of seed after he has sown all his seed satisfactorily over the course of the year.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">The Quadripartitus perhaps read ‘tima’ for ‘cyn’. K: a typo ‘þat’ corrected.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">450</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sed. <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sed. MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">450</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">semitis <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">semitis MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">450</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">glaubte Quadr.</hi> timā <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> cyn <hi rend="italic">zu lesen?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">did Quadr. think he was reading timā instead of cyn?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">450</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lepfulnę <hi rend="italic">M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lepfulnę M</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">251</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ob er ein Freier? Jedenfalls nicht der Aufseher übers Saatkorn (gegen Andrews <hi rend="italic">Manor</hi> 204); <hi rend="italic">s. u</hi>. 17</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Was he a free man? At any rate not the overseer of the seed-corn (against Andrews <hi rend="italic">Manor</hi> 204); <hi rend="italic">see below</hi> 17</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.de1.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">450</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">c.</hi> ¹/₂ (²/₃) Bushel = <hi rend="italic">c.</hi> 18 (24) Liter</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">c.</hi> ¹/₂ (²/₃) bushel = <hi rend="italic">c.</hi> 18 (24) litres</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rect_11.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">251</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Korb 2. a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Korb 2. a</seg></note>
      </div>
